Tea with Nessie — Office (Excel + Word) scaffold
Use the starter files in ../starter_files/:
•	nessie_guests.xlsx — data source (sheet Guests)
•	tea_with_nessie_invitation.docx — letter with <<merge_field>> placeholders
Goal
Produce personalised invitations so each guest is invited to their venue (one of three Loch Ness tea spots), with the correct time, meeting point, cookie flavour, and postal details.
Field map (Excel column → Word placeholder)
Excel header	Word field
courtesy_title	<<courtesy_title>>
first_name	<<first_name>>
last_name	<<last_name>>
venue_name	<<venue_name>>
venue_town	<<venue_town>>
venue_promise	<<venue_promise>>
meeting_point	<<meeting_point>>
tea_date	<<tea_date>>
tea_time	<<tea_time>>
cookie_flavour	<<cookie_flavour>>
rsvp_deadline	<<rsvp_deadline>>
email	<<email>>
street_address	<<street_address>>
town	<<town>>
postcode	<<postcode>>
guest_id	<<guest_id>>

Checklist
1.	Open nessie_guests.xlsx and confirm the Guests sheet headers match the table above.
2.	Open tea_with_nessie_invitation.docx and verify every <<field>> appears.
3.	Run a mail merge (Word → Mailings) or manually prove the logic on 3 sample guests (one per venue) if your lab Word build blocks automated merge.
4.	Save: your working Excel file; your Word template with << >> fields still visible; at least three finished sample letters (one per venue), or the merged output folder.
5.	Write the 3-page plan (see INSTRUCTIONS.docx).
Logic you must explain in the plan
•	How a guest is assigned to a venue (look at the spreadsheet pattern).
•	Why merge-field names must match column headers exactly.
•	How you would catch a missing field or blank row before sending invitations.
•	How the three venues differ (time, meeting point, “Nessie promise”).
